{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1407772-what-is-a-rule-you-accidentally-overlooked-only-to-discover-your-mistake-too-late","id":1407772,"title":"What is a rule you accidentally overlooked only to discover your mistake too late?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-12T13:50:32-07:00","id":1407772,"title":"What is a rule you accidentally overlooked only to discover your mistake too late?","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Currently reading through the CTL rule book and was skimming a lot. (I am trying to get a game prepared on short notice)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I didn\u2019t really read the Character Creation rules, I skipped to the quick reference. So it surprised me when I was going through Huntsman NPC creation rules that there is a section about bypassing the Seasonal Court protections with loopholes.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">So I went back to the court sections that I skimmed through and saw \u201cOh Fae creatures behave differently to Freeholds depending on what Season it is.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022 Spring - A Fae can only attack if its target is someone they truly covet. (ie a Favorite Escaped Changeling)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022 Summer - Fae cannot retreat.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022 Autumn - Fae must announce themselves before attacking; stronger Fae need to do this further in advance.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022 Winter - Fae must mourn after killing allowing the Changelings to attack while the guard is down.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This really changes up how I was expecting to run my game. But leads to interesting world building/possibilities for future sessions.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:59:42-07:00","id":1409215,"title":"","content":"Specifically, it's how Fae creatures behave <i>in places where the Seasonal Courts hold sway</i>. That's an important distinction. Freeholds with other Court structures would have different bargains and thus different protections. Also, the protections specifically call out &quot;The Gentry and their agents,&quot; which is nebulous but doesn't count every Fae creature ever. Unaligned Hobgoblins, rival Freeholds, Bridge Burners, ancient Arcadian beasts from the dawn of time, and even possibly some Privateers might not have to abide by those restrictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T15:44:46-07:00","id":1409240,"title":"","content":"Way long time ago I thought ones subtracted from successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T19:47:21-07:00","id":1409267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1407772-what-is-a-rule-you-accidentally-overlooked-only-to-discover-your-mistake-too-late?p=1409240#post1409240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Way long time ago I thought ones subtracted from successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s an Old World of Darkness thing, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T14:10:39-07:00","id":1409415,"title":"","content":"I've met a lot of Players or GM's running Demon the decent who miss the rules for <u><b>Supernatural Bulwark</b></u><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T14:23:01-07:00","id":1409417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1407772-what-is-a-rule-you-accidentally-overlooked-only-to-discover-your-mistake-too-late?p=1409267#post1409267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s an Old World of Darkness thing, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, I think I got it from Orpheus.<br /> <br /> It became basically the only way to get Dramatic Failures throughout first edition. Because generally if our group knew they had a negative dicepool they would just decide on another action. So I figured it was part of the rules, but it was just some artifact I carried over from another game. Second edition's 'choosing Dramatic Failures' is a nicer way to get them into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-20-2020, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"http